<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n106083" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Τῠφωεύς</span></b> , ὁ, gen.
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">έος</span>
		<i><span class="en">
			Il.
			2.783
		</span></i>, dat. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">έϊ</span> ib.<i><span class="en">
			782
		</span></i>, acc. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">έα</span>
		<i><span class="en">
			Hes.
			<u>Th.</u>
			821
		</span></i>; <b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Τῡφώς</span></b> , <i><span class="en">
			Pi.
			<u>P.</u>
			1.16
		</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
			A.
			<u>Pr.</u>
			372
		</span></i>, gen.<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b>
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Τυφῶ</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Id.
					<u>Th.</u>
					517
				</span></i>
			, <i><span class="en">
				<u>Supp.</u>
				560
			</span></i> (lyr.), <i><span class="en">
				Ar.
				<u>Nu.</u>
				336
			</span></i> (anap.), acc. 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Τυφῶ</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Hdt.
					3.5
				</span></i>
			, <i><span class="en">
				Ar.
				<u>Eq.</u>
				511
			</span></i> (anap.); also nom. <b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Τῡφῶν</span></b>  (q. v.):—<i>Typhoëus</i> or
				<i>Typhos,</i> a hundred-headed giant buried by Zeus (<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">εἰν Ἀρίμοις</span>), <i><span class="en">
				Il.
				2.782
			</span></i>; youngest son of Gaia and Tartarus, <i><span class="en">
				Hes.
				<u>Th.</u>
				821
			</span></i>; <i><span class="en">
				Pi.
			</span></i> gives his birthplace as Cilicia, but places him under Cyme
			and Sicily, and so accounts for the eruptions of Etna, l.c. [<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ῡ</span> in disyll. cases, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ῠ</span> in the others, cf. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Τυφῶν.</span>]</div>
